      "id": "requests_ndjson",
      "corpus_id": "requests",
      "corpus": ".cache/corpora/requests",
      "repo_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests",
      "revision": "611c6162cbc4ac2020a2f91c7cfa4f3abf9bbb60",
      "source_root": "src/requests",
      "license_path": "benchmarks/REQUESTS_LICENSE.txt",
      "prompt": "Add lazy newline-delimited JSON consumption to Requests through Response.iter_json_lines(chunk_size=512, skip_blank=True). Yield any normal JSON value while reading incrementally from the response's decoded byte stream, not buffering Response.content. Decode NDJSON as UTF-8 regardless of a conflicting response charset; accept a UTF-8 BOM only at the start of the first physical line. Recognize LF and CRLF, including delimiters and UTF-8 characters split across chunks. By default skip whitespace-only lines; skip_blank=False must report them as malformed JSON. Empty input yields nothing, a final non-newline-terminated record is parsed, and a trailing newline must not create a phantom extra record. chunk_size must be a positive non-boolean integer and skip_blank a boolean; invalid arguments raise ValueError before reading. Use the existing JSON decoder's ordinary value semantics.\n\nExpose the same JSONLineDecodeError class as requests.JSONLineDecodeError and requests.exceptions.JSONLineDecodeError, deriving from InvalidJSONError. Malformed JSON or UTF-8 must raise it with a one-based physical line_number (including skipped lines), the original line bytes without its LF/CRLF delimiter in line, the response and its request in the existing exception context attributes, and the original decoding exception as __cause__. A malformed later record must fail only when iteration reaches it. Support already cached responses without changing ordinary json(), iter_lines(), or iter_content() behavior. Add regression tests in new test files, preserving existing tests; local loopback HTTP fixtures are allowed.",
      "base_kind": "pinned_upstream_without_new_feature",
      "preparation_patch": null,
