      "prompt": "Make Click atomic output files behave as transactions across direct click.open_file context managers and command file parameters, for eager, explicitly lazy, and default-lazy opening. On normal completion commit the temporary output; while the callback is running, an existing destination remains unchanged. If a direct file-context body raises, or a command callback fails or exits with a nonzero code, discard the temporary file and preserve the original destination (or leave a new destination absent). A zero-code Click command exit counts as success and must commit. Unused lazy output must remain unopened. Support text and binary files, preserve an existing destination's permissions, close owned handles and make repeated close harmless. Explicit successful close remains a commit.\n\nResources registered with a Click context must receive the actual exception on error, with nesting still deferring cleanup until the outermost exit and the current-context stack restored after success or failure. Preserve callback exceptions. A missing temporary file during abort is harmless; if other abort cleanup fails, retain the primary callback exception and make the cleanup problem discoverable through exception notes or chaining. A clean-completion commit failure such as FileNotFoundError must propagate and give the CLI a failing exit, never be silently converted to success. Preserve ordinary non-atomic file behavior and never close caller-owned standard streams. Add new regression test files without changing existing tests.",
