      "id": "starlette_body_limits",
      "corpus_id": "starlette",
      "corpus": ".cache/corpora/starlette",
      "repo_url": "https://github.com/encode/starlette",
      "revision": "4d72fd87ea1c358691a19468168f7217d8ca6a87",
      "source_root": "starlette",
      "license_path": "benchmarks/STARLETTE_LICENSE.txt",
      "prompt": "Add bounded HTTP request-body buffering to Starlette. Request.body(max_bytes=None) remains unlimited by default and accepts None or a non-negative non-boolean integer; other values raise ValueError before receive is called. Count actual body bytes across all received chunks. Exact-boundary and empty zero-budget bodies succeed. On the first crossing stop reading, do not cache a partial body, and raise public starlette.exceptions.RequestBodyTooLarge, a subclass of HTTPException with status_code 413, limit and received (the cumulative count at the first crossing). Applying a stricter bound to an already cached body must also reject it, without rereading the stream. Preserve ClientDisconnect and normal body/json caching behavior. No ability to reread a rejected partial stream is promised.\n\nProvide starlette.middleware.body_limit.RequestBodyLimitMiddleware(app, max_bytes). For bounded HTTP requests, buffer only up to the first observed crossing before invoking the downstream app. Reject oversize input with a plain-text 413 response whose body is exactly \"Request body too large\", never calling the downstream app or consuming later chunks. For accepted bodies replay exactly those bytes to the downstream receive stream, allowing body/json helpers and repeated cached body reads to work; after the replay delegate subsequent receives such as disconnect to the original receive. Count observed bytes rather than trusting Content-Length. None disables buffering and the limit; websocket and lifespan scopes pass through without reads. Validate the middleware limit at construction. Preserve endpoint failures through the original HTTP TestClient integration with both asyncio and Trio; do not bypass or weaken existing integration tests. Add new regression tests in new test files; local test clients are allowed.",
